    "The AI Project Cycle is a structured five-stage framework for developing any AI project: Problem Scoping, Data Acquisition, Data Exploration, Modelling, and Evaluation.",
    "Problem Scoping is the first and most critical stage where the problem is clearly defined — what needs to be solved, who is affected, and what success looks like.",
    "The 4Ws framework (Who, What, Where, Why) is used during problem scoping to thoroughly understand the problem from all perspectives before jumping to solutions.",
    "Data Acquisition is the second stage where relevant data is collected from various sources such as surveys, sensors, databases, APIs, web scraping, or open datasets.",
    "Data can be structured (organized in tables/databases like CSV or Excel) or unstructured (images, text, audio, video) — both types are valuable for AI projects.",
