    "Generative AI refers to artificial intelligence systems that can create new content — including text, images, audio, video, and code — by learning patterns and structures from vast amounts of existing training data.",
    "Large Language Models (LLMs) like GPT, Gemini, and Claude are neural networks trained on massive text corpora that can understand context, follow instructions, answer questions, write essays, and engage in human-like conversation.",
    "The Transformer architecture, introduced in the 2017 paper 'Attention Is All You Need', is the foundational deep learning model behind modern LLMs — it uses self-attention mechanisms to process and relate all parts of input text simultaneously rather than sequentially.",
    "ChatGPT works by predicting the most probable next token (word or subword) given all preceding tokens, using patterns learned during training on billions of text documents — it does not truly 'understand' meaning but generates statistically coherent responses.",
    "AI image generators like DALL-E and Stable Diffusion create images from text descriptions (prompts) using diffusion models that learn to gradually transform random noise into coherent images matching the given text input.",
    "Prompt engineering is the practice of carefully crafting input instructions to get the best possible output from generative AI — techniques include providing clear context, specifying format, giving examples (few-shot prompting), and iteratively refining prompts.",
    "Hallucinations are a critical limitation of generative AI where the model produces confident-sounding but factually incorrect, fabricated, or nonsensical information because it generates based on statistical patterns rather than verified knowledge.",
